With further research, it may prove to be a new frontier of our knowledge.

00:46:38.160 --> 00:46:41.120
At the Fermi National Accelerator Laboratory near Chicago,

00:46:41.720 --> 00:46:44.970
we are being brought ever closer to an ultimate frontier.

00:46:47.820 --> 00:46:49.660
With huge exotic equipment,

00:46:49.980 --> 00:46:52.920
scientists are working to better see and understand

00:46:52.920 --> 00:46:57.470
the smallest possible particles of which all matter is made.

00:47:00.000 --> 00:47:08.770
Only 25 years ago, atoms composed of protons, neutrons, and electrons were regarded as the smallest basic objects.

00:47:10.370 --> 00:47:15.070
Today it seems that atoms are built of even tinier things called quarks.

00:47:15.350 --> 00:47:29.950
The Fermilab is in a sense the world's largest and most powerful microscope, an awesome collection of machines.

00:47:30.000 --> 00:47:38.420
designed to shatter atoms to pieces and see the objects within. Buried

00:47:38.420 --> 00:47:42.560
underground, a four-mile ring of powerful magnets guides a narrow beam of

00:47:42.560 --> 00:47:48.040
particles which is rapidly accelerated. When fired at their target, they will act

00:47:48.040 --> 00:47:56.960
like a powerful hammer to break an atom apart. The process begins with a giant

00:47:56.960 --> 00:47:59.330
generator and a massive jolt of power.

00:48:05.240 --> 00:48:07.620
Hurled within seconds to nearly the speed of light,

00:48:08.300 --> 00:48:11.460
the beam of particles is aimed to strike the tiny nuclei of atom.

00:48:12.510 --> 00:48:15.290
The collision will be photographed by several sensitive cameras.

00:48:30.000 --> 00:48:38.050
Projected onto an analyzing table, the resulting pictures show the scattered tracks left by hundreds of liberated subatomic particles.

00:48:43.170 --> 00:48:48.420
Each type of particle has its own distinguishing signature of curving or spinning lines.

00:48:52.060 --> 00:48:59.590
By carefully recording and studying these trails, we are gradually learning more about the now smallest and most elusive units of matter.

00:49:00.350 --> 00:49:03.130
The still unseen entities called quarks.

00:49:05.500 --> 00:49:08.520
Quarks, however, may well be composed of even smaller things.

00:49:09.430 --> 00:49:14.630
We still do not know where, or if ever, the world of the small will stop.

