00:50:31.600 --> 00:50:37.550
Powerful instruments like the Mayall telescope are now seeing the heavens more clearly than has ever been possible.

00:50:40.230 --> 00:50:47.720
Its light-collecting mirror can photographically detect objects more than six million times fainter than the unaided eye can see.

00:50:53.780 --> 00:50:56.820
Astronomers today rarely look through a telescope directly.

00:51:03.200 --> 00:51:11.340
An array of computers and image intensifiers record and make visible objects that the eye alone is not sensitive enough to see.

00:51:15.830 --> 00:51:20.290
